---
/** Synthetic teaching example: each system's within-group accuracy stays fixed. */
---
<div class="widget-wrap" id="evaluation-mix">
  <p class="widget-eyebrow">Survey-response classification</p>
  <p class="widget-title">How the task mix changes the ranking</p>
  <p class="widget-intro">Two systems classify survey answers with different strengths: A gets 90% of explicit answers right and 50% of ambiguous answers, while B gets 80% of each right. Adjusting the proportion of explicit answers changes their overall scores while keeping these within-group accuracies fixed.</p>
  <label for="eval-mix">Explicit answers in the test set <output id="eval-mix-value" for="eval-mix">80%</output></label>
  <input id="eval-mix" type="range" min="0" max="100" step="5" value="80" />
  <div class="mix-scale"><span>All ambiguous</span><span>All explicit</span></div>
  <div class="mix-results" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
    <div class="mix-row"><span>System A</span><div class="mix-track"><span id="eval-a-bar" style="width:82%"></span></div><strong id="eval-a">82%</strong></div>
    <div class="mix-row mix-row--b"><span>System B</span><div class="mix-track"><span id="eval-b-bar" style="width:80%"></span></div><strong id="eval-b">80%</strong></div>
    <p id="eval-verdict">System A leads by 2 percentage points.</p>
    <p id="eval-calculation">A: 0.80 × 90% + 0.20 × 50% = 82%. B: 80% in either group.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="visual-diagram__caption">Because the systems' within-group performance stays fixed, the change in ranking comes entirely from the mix of answers being measured. The scores tie at 75% explicit answers, with B leading below that point. These rates are invented to illustrate task mix, without modelling sampling uncertainty.</p>
  <noscript><p>At 20% explicit answers, A scores 58% and B scores 80%. At 80% explicit answers, A scores 82% and B scores 80%.</p></noscript>
</div>
<script>
  const root = document.getElementById('evaluation-mix');
  if (root) {
    const slider = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#eval-mix')!;
    const setText = (selector: string, text: string) => { root.querySelector(selector)!.textContent = text; };
    const update = () => {
      const fraction = Number(slider.value) / 100;
      const score = 50 + 40 * fraction;
      setText('#eval-mix-value', `${slider.value}%`);
      setText('#eval-a', `${score.toFixed(0)}%`);
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#eval-a-bar')!.style.width = `${score}%`;
      const difference = score - 80;
      setText('#eval-verdict', difference === 0 ? 'The systems tie at 80% overall accuracy.' : `System ${difference > 0 ? 'A' : 'B'} leads by ${Math.abs(difference).toFixed(0)} percentage points.`);
      setText('#eval-calculation', `A: ${fraction.toFixed(2)} × 90% + ${(1 - fraction).toFixed(2)} × 50% = ${score.toFixed(0)}%. B: 80% in either group.`);
    };
    slider.addEventListener('input', update);
  }
</script>
<style>
  label { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; }
  output { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 16px; }
  input { width: 100%; margin: 18px 0 8px; accent-color: var(--c-a); cursor: pointer; }
  input:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--c-a); outline-offset: 4px; }
  .mix-scale { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 11px; }
  .mix-results { margin-top: 26px; }
  .mix-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 75px minmax(0, 1fr) 42px; gap: 12px; align-items: center; margin: 15px 0; font-size: 12px; }
  .mix-track { height: 20px; border-radius: 3px; background: var(--border-lt); overflow: hidden; }
  .mix-track span { display: block; height: 100%; background: var(--c-a); }
  .mix-row--b .mix-track span { background: var(--c-b); }
  #eval-verdict { font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 6px; }
  #eval-calculation { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-sec); }
</style>
